From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:43:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_bcm: Add iPhone 6s Plus BCM4350C5

Match the iPhone 6s Plus BCM4350C5 with the plain hci_bcm sequence that
starts the iPad Air 2's BCM4350C2: Patchram at 115,200 baud, then the
board's max-speed. Untested on the N66 so far.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
index 1918caf00..672ddf1da 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
@@ -1754,6 +1754,8 @@ static const struct of_device_id bcm_bluetooth_of_match[] = {
 	  .data = &bcm4355_j172_device_data },
 	/* The iPad Air 2 BCM4350C2 runs the plain sequence at 115,200 baud. */
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j81-bcm4350c2-bt" },
+	/* The iPhone 6s Plus BCM4350C5, as the iPad Air 2's C2 so far. */
+	{ .compatible = "apple,n66-bcm4350c5-bt" },
 	/* The iPod touch 6 BCM4345B1 uses the plain sequence at 115,200 baud. */
 	{ .compatible = "apple,n102-bcm4345b1-bt" },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j71b-bcm4355c1-bt",
